---
description: Core safety guardrails for code modernization initiatives.
alwaysApply: true
---

- Separate behavior-preserving refactoring from structural rearchitecting.
- Require baseline characterization tests before modifying legacy logic.
- Require an approved Architecture Decision Record (ADR) and explicit interface contracts before extracting services or splitting shared databases.
- Follow the safety rules of every stack profile in scope. For example, mainframe records are converted field by field from copybook layouts, never as whole-record text, and packed or zoned decimals never pass through floating point.
